<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<Title>TestFramework.Core</Title>
		<Authors>DeadMoon0</Authors>
		<Product>TestFramework</Product>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageTags>Test;UnitTest;IntegrationTest;Framework;Fluent;Timeline</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<Description>The core package of the TestFramework ecosystem for building integration-style and end-to-end test workflows. Provides the timeline engine for steps, events, variables, artifacts, retries, timeouts, and assertions, and serves as the foundation for extension packages like Azure, LocalIO, and Simple.</Description>
		<Version>0.2.0</Version>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/DeadMoon0/TestFramework-Core.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) DeadMoon0 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Performance: the debug pipe is no longer attached unconditionally, removing a ~2s stall from every run (test suites that paid it are roughly an order of magnitude faster). Set TESTFRAMEWORK_DEBUG_PIPE=on to force it, off to disable it.
Security: the debug pipe client now uses CurrentUserOnly, and both the breakpoint wait and the pipe write are bounded so an unresponsive UI can no longer stall a run.
Run isolation: an artifact reference is now copied per run, so two runs of one timeline no longer share pinned state. A frozen run is now genuinely immutable.
Fixes: VariableReference.Transform no longer recurses into a StackOverflow; ConstVariable.Transform no longer drops an existing transform chain; FreezableCollection.Contains no longer throws once frozen; SequentialEvent honours cancellation instead of polling on; OutputRunDebugger is safe under parallel steps; a step timeout no longer leaves the abandoned attempt racing its own retry.
Usability: reusing a run builder throws TimelineRunBuilderAlreadyUsedException instead of failing obscurely; immutable-variable enforcement is restored; logging no longer blocks the calling step.
Also adds PersistentEnvironmentContext.CreateAsync as a non-blocking alternative to the constructor, which is now obsolete.</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="..\Modules\TestFramework-Common\Assets\Icon.png">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Config.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Core.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
		<AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
			<_Parameter1>TestFramework.Simple.Tests</_Parameter1>
		</AssemblyAttribute>
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="xunit.abstractions" Version="2.0.3" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
	  <None Include="README.md">
	    <Pack>True</Pack>
	    <PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
	  </None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
